ght being 2020 it was a  mistake well i hear you 100 because it's  not as simple as just playing an idol it  also matters what statement is made at  tribal council and i do want to rewind a  little bit because when drea was voted  out she made quite the statement about  you she kind of threw you under the bus  so do you think that drea's parting  words affected your game yeah it's  really hard to know um  how a subjective thing like that  translates to  you know  objective effect i suppose i would say i  think that for mike and jonathan it  really had nothing to do with it because  the reason jonathan turned on me was  that i shared information about an  advantage to the idol nullifier with  lindsay  and that's something that he and i had  shared together so by breaking his trust  by telling her  he realized lindsay and i were closer  and he decided to go separate ways from  me and he told mike about the nullifier  and mike turned on me and then with  marianne the words treya had and as well  as seeing me hand the idol back to mike  because mike insisted it happened right  away after we got back and i was like we  should be more discreet but he's like  not right now and so i handed it back to  him and she saw that and i think that  was really jarring for her because she  realized i was playing a bigger game  than i um  had led on up until that point so i  think you know it probably played a  partial role with marianne maybe  solidified a role with the other two i  think it's very probable that it would  have been me regardless um and i don't  have any hard feelings for her saying  that because when i made the move  against her i knew that that's something  that could happen because it's not  against the rules  well i i do want to ask about your  relationship with marianne because on  twitter we've asked fans if they have  any questions for you and um  so frank frankenwenz asked did you ever  consider that marianne might use her  extra vote against you  it's so um i 